      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In conclusion, the teaching program we developed appears to meet the needs originally established by the audit. Nurses are provided with a method of assessment, evaluation, and documentation. The program also provides a means of teaching continuity while following a structured time schedule that allows for recognition and satisfaction of individual patient needs. The patient teaching record provides the final tool as a reference and ongoing source of evaluation."},
